---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout basePath="" title="The Pattern Trap | Manifesto">
  <section class="pt-32 pb-16 px-4 bg-brand-light-bg text-center border-b border-brand-border">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-brand-saffron font-bold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-6 text-sm md:text-base">
        The Manifesto
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-extrabold text-brand-navy mb-6 tracking-tight">The Illusion of Free Will.</h1>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-brand-text leading-relaxed font-medium">
        You think you are making choices. But if you look closely at your life over the last ten years, you aren't making choices. You are running a script.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-24 px-4 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-lg prose-slate prose-headings:text-brand-navy prose-a:text-brand-saffron hover:prose-a:text-brand-saffron-dark">
      <p class="lead text-2xl font-serif text-brand-navy mb-10 leading-relaxed border-l-4 border-brand-saffron pl-6">
        Every January, millions of people decide to change their lives. They read books, they set goals, they wake up at 5 AM. And by February, 90% of them are exactly where they started.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">Why does this happen?</h2>
      <p>
        We are sold a lie by the self-help industry. The lie is that your problems are caused by a lack of discipline, a lack of knowledge, or a lack of motivation. 
      </p>
      <p>
        But you already know what you should be doing. You know how to eat better. You know you shouldn't text that person back. You know you should start that business. You have the knowledge. You have the desire.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>So why don't you do it?</strong>
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">The Pattern Trap</h2>
      <p>
        Beneath your conscious desires, there is an operating system. A behavioral blueprint that was coded into you long before you had the ability to choose it.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you try to change your life using willpower, you are fighting your own operating system. It is a war you will inevitably lose, because willpower is finite, but your pattern is infinite. It runs quietly in the background, 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.
      </p>

      <div class="bg-brand-navy text-white p-8 rounded-2xl my-12 shadow-lg">
        <h3 class="text-brand-saffron text-xl font-bold mb-4 mt-0">The symptoms of an active pattern:</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-4 mb-0">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-saffron">✦</span> Dating different people who all end up hurting you in the exact same way.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-saffron">✦</span> Switching jobs repeatedly but always hitting the same invisible ceiling.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-saffron">✦</span> Sabotaging your own success right before you finally get what you want.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-brand-saffron">✦</span> Feeling a chronic, unexplainable exhaustion even when you haven't done anything.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">You Cannot Fix What You Cannot See</h2>
      <p>
        You are stuck in a loop. And the defining characteristic of a loop is that when you are inside it, it just feels like "life." It feels like bad luck. It feels like circumstances. 
      </p>
      <p>
        But it isn't. It's an algorithm. A predictable set of emotional reactions and behavioral defaults that lead to the exact same outcomes, year after year.
      </p>
      <p>
        The only way out of a loop is to step outside of it and look at the code. You must map the pattern. You must see the uncomfortable truth about why you are building your own prison.
      </p>

      <div class="text-center mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-brand-border">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6">Stop fighting the symptoms. Diagnose the root.</h3>
        <a href="/get-reading" class="inline-block px-8 py-4 bg-brand-saffron text-white rounded-xl font-bold text-lg hover:scale-105 transition-transform shadow-md">
          Diagnose My Pattern
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
